<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mempawah</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mempawah is a coastal town in West Kalimantan, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, north of Pontianak, and the seat of a regency of the same name. It was the centre of a Malay sultanate linked by marriage to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bugis">Bugis</a> and Arab families. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syarif-abdurrahman-alkadrie">Syarif Abdurrahman Alkadrie</a>, founder of Pontianak, was the son of an Arab cleric who had settled there.</p></div>
